Description: StreamPlayer: re-target playback to media2's sound player
 Upstream configured a legacy BMediaFile over the stream and drove a
 legacy BSoundPlayer from it. media2's BSoundPlayer takes a BMediaFormat
 and its GetVolumeInfo no longer carries a media_node, so the player
 half is retargeted accordingly. The decode half stops at the decoder
 V\OS does not have for byte streams: media2's BMediaFile opens an
 entry_ref or a BUrl only (its decode path is excluded for this port)
 and BMediaDecoder is video-only, so _OpenDecoder() reports
 B_UNSUPPORTED and the state machine stops with the stream shut down.
 The media_header/media_decode_info/media_codec_info members go with the
 extractor; media2's headers do not define them.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: vendor
Last-Update: 2026-10-21
